# This package is NOT meant to be stowed, and this file is the guard.
#
# clauth rewrites ~/.clauth/profiles.toml in place (profile ordering, the
# active marker), which destroys a stow symlink and leaves the repo copy
# stale — the same failure mode as Claude Code's settings.json. The file is
# bootstrap-copied by _install/clauth.sh and synced back with
# `just clauth-sync`.
#
# Without this ignore, an accidental `stow clauth` would symlink profiles.toml
# into the repo and cause exactly the breakage the copy pattern avoids, since
# ~/.clauth already exists as a real directory and stow would descend into it.
profiles\.toml

# Docs (local ignore overrides the global one, so re-list essentials)
^/README.*
AGENTS\.md
